 "checkpoint": "The Death of Ismāʿīl",
 "note": "Four days after the Emperor Ismāʿīl II died in camp at Ishbīliya, on 28 June 1429, after twenty-four years on the throne. His son Muḥammad V, forty-three, reigns; the heir is Muḥammad's eldest son Ismāʿīl, and Ismāʿīl and his brother Aḥmad now sit in the dīwān. The succession has cost the crown most of its political influence (22, from 100). The crown holds 195 towns and 2,571,000 people, with seven ṭāʾifas; Teguise on Lanzarote was settled on 1 July. The Angevin Empire, Castile's ally, is second in the world with 180 points to al-Andalus's 101. Estates estimated from the reading of 16 November 1428. Treasury 647 with 565 owed; income 280 against 295; stability 6.",
